      "comment": "MISS CHEVALIER (4) is resuming after two soft-track Morphettville runs that read well for this: a debut second in BM64 company, then a fourth when odds-on, beaten a length and a half after racing keenly and wide throughout. An easy Oakbank trial win under her belt and she should be primed for a big run. FEAR THE ZOU (3) is the race-fit danger after a much better Gawler third, beaten just under two lengths, and the 1.5kg claim is useful. Can threaten. TWOPENNIE (7) brings no race form but has trialled sharply, winning over 600m then going under by 0.21 in a 1000m Murray Bridge trial, so appeals from barrier 1. Watch the betting. TOP SORT (10) is facing the starter for the first time. By Tassort and comes from the Jessica Tzaferis stable. Top-three chance.",
